    {
      "order": 2,
      "type": "feature",
      "purpose": "Show the four concrete things a gated checklist does that a written runbook cannot, so the reader stops comparing us to a document.",
      "module": "../../modules/feature/feature-matrix-grid",
      "moduleId": "feature-matrix-grid",
      "variants": {
        "layoutArchetype": "grid",
        "density": "compact",
        "backgroundBleed": "surface-contained",
        "motion": "none",
        "artDirection": "data-led"
      },
      "content": {
        "sectionLabel": "What a gate actually does",
        "headline": "Four things your runbook cannot do on its own",
        "body": "A document can list the steps. It cannot stop a release when step three was never done, and it cannot tell you six weeks later who decided that was fine at the time. That gap is the whole product.",
        "featureItems": [
          [
            "Steps that refuse to be skipped",
            "Gate four stays shut until gate three carries a name and a timestamp. Nobody reorders the list halfway through a release, and nobody has to be the person who notices."
          ],
          [
            "One named owner per step",
            "Steps are assigned to a person, not to a channel. Holdpoint nudges them in Slack and keeps nudging until they check it off or hand it to someone who will."
          ],
          [
            "An audit trail that writes itself",
            "Every check-off stores the person, the commit SHA, the environment and the clock time. Export the release as CSV or PDF the week your SOC 2 evidence request lands."
          ],
          [
            "Rollback lives in the same list",
            "The undo steps sit in the runbook already gated, so the 2am version of you is reading a checklist instead of inventing one."
          ]
        ]
      },
      "selectionReason": "case-saas-release selected feature-matrix-grid: Four capabilities that are meant to be read against each other, not scrolled through one at a time — a matrix keeps them on one surface and gives the lead item the room it needs.",
